    "answer": {
      "state": "completed",
      "text": "Decision for the discharge plan: Priya Tanaka (Ward 4, Bed 14, day 6) is medically ready for discharge, but she should not be discharged home unsupported now. Record the disposition as \"Home with support, once a carer arrangement is in place.\" She stays on the ward until that support is confirmed.\n\nJustification:\n- **Medically ready:** She has been clinically stable for 24 hours. All bloods are back and no investigations are outstanding. Her discharge medications have been reconciled against her home list, with no changes and no interactions.\n- **Unsafe to go home alone:** She needs a frame to walk and someone with her on stairs. She has no one at home and no carer arrangement in place.\n- **Her wishes:** She has said several times that she wants to go home, so the plan aims for home rather than an alternative placement. The evidence does not show any reason to rule home out once support exists.\n\nConditions before discharge:\n1. A carer or support arrangement is in place that covers her mobility needs, including help on stairs.\n2. An outpatient follow-up appointment is booked. None is booked yet, and the clinic has not confirmed one.\n\nNot established by the evidence:\n- Whether a formal care package or carer support can be arranged, or how quickly.\n- Whether her daughter, Mira, can provide support.\n- Her home layout, such as whether there are stairs at home.\n\nIf support at home cannot be arranged, the disposition will need to be revisited. That should involve the social worker, the physiotherapist, the consultant, and Priya and her daughter.",
